<article class="env-lemma" id="0A6K">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0A6K">Lemma <span data-tag="0A6K">15.90.5</span>.</a> Let $I$ be a finitely generated ideal of a ring $R$. The $I$-power torsion modules form a Serre subcategory of the abelian category $\text{Mod}_ R$, see Homology, Definition <a href="/tag/02MO" data-tag="02MO">12.10.1</a>. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      It is clear that a submodule and a quotient module of an $I$-power torsion module is $I$-power torsion. Moreover, the extension of two $I$-power torsion modules is $I$-power torsion by Lemma <a href="/tag/05EB" data-tag="05EB">15.90.4</a>. Hence the statement of the lemma by Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/02MP" data-tag="02MP">12.10.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>